<title>BELGIUM: Arthuis says confident on EU stability pact accord.</title>
<headline>Arthuis says confident on EU stability pact accord.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Finance Minister Jean Arthuis said on Sunday he was confident the European Union would be able to reach an agreement on a budget stability pact at summit of EU leaders in Dublin next month.</p>
<p>&quot;We have to find an agreement. I am quite confident,&quot; he told Reuters Financial Television.</p>
<p>He had been asked whether EU leaders would be able to agree in Dublin on the stability pact, which is meant to ensure countries joining European monetary union maintain fiscal discipline in the years beyond its launch.</p>
<p>Talks on the stability pact have run into disagreements however over the kind of exceptional circumstances which would justify a country running up a slightly larger budget deficit. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
